## NeurIPS rebuttal runs — Reviewer zvRY (scripts added 2026-07-28)

Five scripts added under `mtil/scripts/11task/rebuttal_*.sh`, plus analysis
tooling in `mtil/scripts/rebuttal/` (see its README). Each training run is
`phase3_no_lora_11t_v4.sh` with exactly one flag changed, so every row is a
single-factor control. Nothing in `src/` or `scripts/4task/phase3/` was
modified; the control axes are monkey-patched in at run time.

| Run | Answers | Save dir | Status |
|---|---|---|---|
| `rebuttal_replay_only_matched.sh` (λ=0, v4 iters) | Q1 per-task baseline | `/scratch/.../rebuttal_replay_only_matched` | done, job 18943387 |
| `rebuttal_zeroshot_eval.sh` | Q1 "close to CLIP pretraining" | `/scratch/.../rebuttal/zeroshot` | done, job 18943385 |
| `rebuttal_rd_current_images_noZSCL.sh` (C1b) | Q2 current-task images | `/scratch/.../rebuttal_rd_current_images_noZSCL` | done, job 18943392 |
| `rebuttal_rd_prev_teacher_noZSCL.sh` (C2b) | Q3 previous-task teacher | `/scratch/.../rebuttal_rd_prev_teacher_noZSCL` | done, job 18943389 |
| `rebuttal_rd_current_images.sh` / `_prev_teacher.sh` / `_reference_images.sh` | same questions, ZSCL branch on | — | not run (≤0.4 pt ceiling) |

### Results (2026-08-02)

All rows below computed with `scripts/rebuttal/rd_control_table.py`; the two
pre-existing no-ZSCL rows reproduce 66.72 / 64.38 exactly, confirming one
metric definition across the table.

| Run | Last | Avg | Transfer |
|---|---|---|---|
| ExRD, λ=0.3 (headline) | 86.17 | 87.15 | 68.37 |
| Replay only, λ=0, iteration-matched | **86.83** | 87.12 | 68.17 |
| Replay only, λ=0, uniform 1500 it. (old row) | 86.44 | 86.95 | 68.00 |
| ZSCL only, no replay | 83.79 | 87.12 | 68.69 |
| no ZSCL: RD on replay, frozen teacher | 86.24 | 87.05 | 66.72 |
| no ZSCL: RD on current-task images (C1b) | 86.71 | 86.70 | 66.66 |
| no ZSCL: RD teacher = prev-task ckpt (C2b) | 86.73 | 86.81 | 65.42 |
| no ZSCL: no anchor at all | 86.62 | 86.86 | 64.38 |

**Q3 — the frozen anchor is load-bearing (confirms the paper's claim).** RD's
recovery over no-anchor is 2.34 Transfer; the previous-task teacher recovers
only 1.04, i.e. **56% of RD's benefit is specifically the teacher being the
frozen pre-trained model**. A rolling self-teacher lands nearer to no anchor
than to a frozen one.

**Q2 — the replay images are NOT a core part of RD.** Current-task images
recover 66.66 vs the buffer's 66.72 (0.06 against a 2.34 range) *and* are 0.47
better on Last. In the no-ZSCL block Last is flat (86.24–86.73), so Transfer is
the only moving metric. Implication: the buffer is a label carrier for
L_rep; RD needs some in-domain probe images but not stored ones. This
contradicts the "one minibatch, two orthogonal roles" novelty framing in the
uc1s response, and makes RD-on-current-task-images ≈ MulKI's design point.

**Q1 — RD is a Transfer-for-Last trade, smaller than reported.** Against the
iteration-matched λ=0 baseline: **−0.66 Last, +0.20 Transfer** (the confounded
comparison suggested −0.27 / +0.37). Per task, RD lowers final accuracy on 9/12
eval sets and raises pre-exposure (zero-shot) accuracy on 8/11. The reviewer's
hypothesis is directionally supported: mean Δpre-exposure is +0.31 for the six
high-zero-shot tasks vs −0.12 for the six low ones (Spearman +0.47), but n=11
so this is not statistically significant.

**Action required on the submitted text:** the λ=0 row in the 3U1b sensitivity
table (86.44 / 77.57 / 68.00) is iteration-mismatched and must be replaced by
86.83 / 87.12 / 68.17. Note the matched λ=0 run now has the best Last of any
configuration, so "ExRD leads on Last" needs restating as the λ knob's
Last-optimal endpoint.

### Confound found while building the per-task analysis

The λ=0 row quoted in the rebuttal (86.44 Last / 68.00 Transfer,
`ckpt/11task/ablation_prop_replay`) was trained with **uniform 1500 iters/task**,
but ExRD (`phase3_no_lora_v4`, 86.17 / 68.37) uses the **per-task schedule**
(Aircraft 3000, StanfordCars 3000, SUN397 5000, MNIST 800, ...). The per-task
delta between them therefore mixes RD with an iteration-budget effect:

- Mean ΔLast over the 11 trained tasks is **−0.27**, not positive.
- The two largest apparent RD gains land exactly on the two tasks with the
  biggest iteration advantage: StanfordCars +3.52 (3000 vs 1500) and
  SUN397 +1.82 (5000 vs 1500).
- Where RD does look real on the current numbers: ImageNet Last +0.31 and
  per-task pre-exposure (zero-shot before the task is trained) improves on
  7/11 eval sets, consistent with RD acting on Transfer rather than on Last.

`rebuttal_replay_only_matched.sh` removes the confound and is what
`per_task_rd_analysis.py` expects by default. It also yields an
iteration-matched λ=0 row for the sensitivity table in the Reviewer 3U1b
response.

**Resolved 2026-08-02.** The matched baseline ran; the −0.27 figure above was
the confounded estimate and the true matched value is **−0.66 ΔLast /
+0.20 ΔTransfer**. See the results table above; the numbers in this subsection
are retained only as a record of the confound.
